From 56da5d5d6e83f26339868e43a53ee2c8b3427975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mining: reuse eligible speculative overlays for templates and
 block script checks

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved historical source semantics; canonical regrouping and repairs are recorded separately.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Fast-path single-input CheckRegularTransaction duplicate-input checks,
coalesce BlockUndo disk writes, and optimize bulk mempool clear.

Original-Commit: a4ea86865414bbf4f98512bbd4460e2a42897acc
Original-Patch: ecash/020
Split-Concern: miner

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Canonical-Purpose-Regrouping: Keep the prepared-block fixture with the assembler
root-reuse feature it exercises, rather than as a standalone performance patch.
Additional-Original-Patch: ecash/008
Additional-Split-Id: 9

Plan-v2 owner repair: B2/B3: roots use the actually selected transaction vector; a matching transaction count cannot authorize overlay reuse.

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
0006-overlay-miner-fees-and-limits.patch: Same-purpose introduced defect; original named owner retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.
